    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a001",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Bonds.** `parent` is the parent body's centre-of-mass junction. T carries it to the joint frame (`to_joint`); the joint sits outside, between `to_joint` and `from_joint`. L carries the joint's child side to this body's principal centre-of-mass frame, the 1-junction BJ (`com`), where the body, the next link and the contact points attach.",
        "x": 0,
        "y": -150,
        "w": 640,
        "h": 110,
        "color": "blue"
      },
      {
        "id": "a002",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Pose band.** W = parent_pose o LN o joint_pose is the body frame in the world (`pose`, what the 3D scene reads); P = W o LC is the principal frame (`com_pose`), which the body and the contact points read.",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 540,
        "w": 640,
        "h": 90,
        "color": "blue"
      }
    ]
